  "notes": "Boa Safra Sementes (SOJA3) \u2014 Brazil's #1 independent soybean seed producer (Formosa-GO HQ). IPO on B3 Novo Mercado April 2021 (R$400M primary at R$9.90/share). BRL reporting, calendar fiscal year. Pure-play soybean seed multiplier \u2014 buys foundation seed from licensors (Bayer/BASF/Corteva/GDM), multiplies through contracted growers, conditions, treats, packages and sells to ~10k+ farmers. Revenue is highly seasonal, concentrated in 3T/4T (Sep-Dec planting season for Brazilian soja safra). grossRevenueMM = receita bruta (pre-PIS/COFINS/ICMS), revenueMM = receita l\u00edquida. Expenses split as CPV (custo dos produtos vendidos), G&A (despesas gerais e administrativas), D&A (deprecia\u00e7\u00e3o e amortiza\u00e7\u00e3o), Outras (other opex). 5-year FY history from CVM ITR/DFP filings + ri.boasafra.com.br release decks. Pre-IPO 2020 figures from S-1 (Prospecto Definitivo) and post-IPO restatements. Net debt rose materially 2022-2024 as company built working capital + new processing units (Cristalina-GO, Rio Verde-GO). Receita l\u00edquida 2024 hit by harvest delays + farmer credit stress, FY24 EBITDA margin compressed.",
